---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Website Terms"
  description="Draft website terms for The OC Events Market."
  noindex
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Website Terms</h1>
    <p><strong>Owner and legal review required before production launch.</strong></p>
    <p>
      These draft terms describe general website use only. They are not a contract for event
      planning and do not replace a signed proposal or service agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Website information</h2>
    <p>
      Website copy is provided for general information. Service availability, responsibilities,
      inclusions, staffing, hours on the event day, pricing, and vendor terms are controlled by the
      approved proposal and signed agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>No booking through a text</h2>
    <p>
      A text conversation does not reserve a date, create a client relationship, guarantee
      availability, or confirm a service. A vendor introduction does not create a partnership or
      recommendation.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside services</h2>
    <p>
      Vendors, venues, and linked services may have separate contracts, policies, pricing, licenses,
      and responsibilities. The final terms must reflect the business’s actual contracting model.
    </p>

    <h2>Photography and intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses a mix of licensed editorial photography and owner-provided event-detail media.
      An event image does not by itself establish the planner’s scope, a vendor partnership, or an
      included service. Portfolio facts, publication rights, credits, and permissions must be
      confirmed before complete celebration stories publish.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing terms and contact</h2>
    <p>
      The legal entity, contact details, language about governing law, disclaimer scope, and dispute
      terms remain owner and counsel decisions and are intentionally absent.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
